1
00:00:00,541 --> 00:00:03,104
One scientific workflow can connect

2
00:00:03,224 --> 00:00:04,906
many specialized tools.

3
00:00:05,807 --> 00:00:07,689
Start with organic electronics

4
00:00:07,689 --> 00:00:09,090
and materials research.

5
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:11,191
FreeCAD provides a geometry

6
00:00:11,191 --> 00:00:12,492
and scripting environment.

7
00:00:12,673 --> 00:00:15,275
Its Python interface offers a way to begin

8
00:00:15,275 --> 00:00:17,596
without a dedicated integration server.

9
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:20,579
An agent can help prepare stress, thermal,

10
00:00:20,579 --> 00:00:22,640
airflow, and electrostatic studies.

11
00:00:22,901 --> 00:00:24,862
For example, study heat spreading

12
00:00:24,862 --> 00:00:27,104
through an organic light emitting device.

13
00:00:27,424 --> 00:00:29,105
The selected numerical solver

14
00:00:29,105 --> 00:00:30,506
performs the calculation.

15
00:00:31,487 --> 00:00:34,130
Electronic design
includes digital circuits,

16
00:00:34,391 --> 00:00:35,432
analog circuits,

17
00:00:35,652 --> 00:00:37,194
photonic integrated circuits,

18
00:00:37,194 --> 00:00:38,756
and printed circuit boards.

19
00:00:39,016 --> 00:00:41,419
Each branch needs a suitable tool chain.

20
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:43,942
The agent helps connect the steps,

21
00:00:44,222 --> 00:00:46,285
while the specialized software handles

22
00:00:46,285 --> 00:00:47,406
its part of the work.

23
00:00:48,607 --> 00:00:51,510
In a laboratory, an agent could coordinate

24
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,913
sample handling, instrument control,

25
00:00:54,113 --> 00:00:55,254
mobile navigation,

26
00:00:55,434 --> 00:00:57,436
and camera guided manipulation.

27
00:00:58,037 --> 00:01:00,019
Frameworks such as ROS 2

28
00:01:00,159 --> 00:01:01,640
help connect the pieces.

29
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:04,723
Real hardware also needs suitable drivers,

30
00:01:04,884 --> 00:01:07,246
sensors, and careful safety checks.

31
00:01:08,407 --> 00:01:11,308
Different optics problems
need different models.

32
00:01:11,748 --> 00:01:13,869
Ray tracing supports lens design.

33
00:01:14,309 --> 00:01:17,450
Electromagnetic simulation
describes wave behavior.

34
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:20,831
Periodic diffraction
models help study gratings,

35
00:01:21,171 --> 00:01:24,752
while beam propagation methods
address coherent light.

36
00:01:25,132 --> 00:01:26,453
Choose the modeling approach

37
00:01:26,453 --> 00:01:28,033
to match the physical problem.

38
00:01:29,213 --> 00:01:31,614
The same pattern connects these examples.

39
00:01:31,974 --> 00:01:33,975
The agent coordinates the workflow.

40
00:01:34,335 --> 00:01:36,916
Numerical software
performs the calculations.

41
00:01:37,176 --> 00:01:38,996
Researchers check the assumptions,

42
00:01:39,196 --> 00:01:40,397
inspect the outputs,

43
00:01:40,597 --> 00:01:42,538
and decide what the results support.

44
00:01:42,898 --> 00:01:44,778
That division of work can extend

45
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:46,279
AI assisted computing

46
00:01:46,279 --> 00:01:47,959
across science and engineering.

47
00:01:51,122 --> 00:01:53,551
An AI agent needs a usable interface

48
00:01:53,652 --> 00:01:55,137
to your scientific software.

49
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,681
The software does not have to be

50
00:01:57,681 --> 00:01:58,861
written in Python.

51
00:01:59,201 --> 00:02:01,702
What matters is the interface: a Python

52
00:02:02,023 --> 00:02:05,104
API, a command line, or the application's

53
00:02:05,164 --> 00:02:06,324
own scripting tools.

54
00:02:06,544 --> 00:02:09,306
Available operations and permissions
determine what the

55
00:02:09,306 --> 00:02:10,906
agent can actually automate.

56
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:14,169
That opens the door to tools such

57
00:02:14,169 --> 00:02:17,451
as KiCad, ngspice, FreeCAD, and OpenFOAM.

58
00:02:17,892 --> 00:02:19,733
Each exposes different controls.

59
00:02:20,093 --> 00:02:22,435
Choose the interface the software
supports, and

60
00:02:22,435 --> 00:02:25,097
inspect the inputs and returned files
instead

61
00:02:25,097 --> 00:02:27,299
of assuming every application works the
same

62
00:02:27,299 --> 00:02:27,579
way.

63
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:31,221
When a simulation outgrows your laptop,
the

64
00:02:31,221 --> 00:02:33,723
workflow can extend to an authorized
computing

65
00:02:33,723 --> 00:02:36,304
cluster. An agent can help prepare job

66
00:02:36,304 --> 00:02:39,665
scripts, submit through the scheduler,
monitor progress,

67
00:02:39,705 --> 00:02:41,706
and organize outputs for analysis.

68
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:45,430
For a molecular dynamics example in
GROMACS,

69
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:48,273
prepare the system and minimize its
energy.

70
00:02:48,634 --> 00:02:51,597
Next, establish the intended equilibrium
conditions.

71
00:02:52,138 --> 00:02:54,881
Then run the production simulation and
analyze

72
00:02:54,881 --> 00:02:57,544
the data. Check the inputs and scientific

73
00:02:57,544 --> 00:02:59,186
criteria at each handoff.

74
00:03:00,327 --> 00:03:02,369
Use local SSH authentication.

75
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:05,172
Keep passwords and private keys out of

76
00:03:05,232 --> 00:03:06,253
prompts and logs.

77
00:03:06,453 --> 00:03:09,216
Verify job completion and inspect the
outputs.

78
00:03:09,556 --> 00:03:12,299
Automation does not replace scientific
validation.

79
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,742
Connect through the right interface.

80
00:03:16,002 --> 00:03:17,884
Scale through the right resources.

81
00:03:18,184 --> 00:03:19,806
Keep the science verifiable.

82
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:25,662
AI can help beyond the first simulation
script.

83
00:03:26,042 --> 00:03:28,824
It can also help coordinate what happens next.

84
00:03:29,404 --> 00:03:32,085
The key is to separate building the workflow

85
00:03:32,085 --> 00:03:33,806
from monitoring its progress.

86
00:03:34,907 --> 00:03:37,728
Codex is the engineering assistant in this
example.

87
00:03:38,089 --> 00:03:40,690
It can help write Python and SLURM scripts,

88
00:03:41,050 --> 00:03:42,431
connect permitted tools,

89
00:03:42,431 --> 00:03:44,912
and add file handling and validation checks.

90
00:03:45,232 --> 00:03:47,153
The goal is a reproducible workflow

91
00:03:47,153 --> 00:03:48,553
for the researcher to review.

92
00:03:49,513 --> 00:03:53,975
For GROMACS, that workflow moves from system
preparation

93
00:03:53,975 --> 00:03:57,016
to energy minimization, equilibration,

94
00:03:57,176 --> 00:03:59,117
production dynamics, and analysis.

95
00:03:59,677 --> 00:04:01,498
Scripts organize these stages;

96
00:04:01,838 --> 00:04:03,779
the researcher still checks the model,

97
00:04:03,779 --> 00:04:04,939
settings, and results.

98
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:08,443
Dot provides the coordination role.

99
00:04:08,783 --> 00:04:10,785
With a permitted status integration

100
00:04:10,826 --> 00:04:12,447
or scheduled report configured,

101
00:04:12,908 --> 00:04:15,530
it can follow progress, flag failures,

102
00:04:15,711 --> 00:04:17,512
and bring back completed results.

103
00:04:18,153 --> 00:04:19,875
Define what it should monitor,

104
00:04:19,995 --> 00:04:20,916
when it should check,

105
00:04:21,377 --> 00:04:23,579
and which changes need your attention.

106
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:28,682
Keep credentials in approved local or cluster
secret storage.

107
00:04:28,942 --> 00:04:30,963
Share sanitized status information,

108
00:04:31,163 --> 00:04:33,404
and keep scientific decisions with the
researcher.

109
00:04:33,645 --> 00:04:35,105
Codex builds the workflow.

110
00:04:35,105 --> 00:04:36,486
Dot helps keep it moving.

111
00:04:36,486 --> 00:04:37,506
You remain in control.

112
00:04:38,706 --> 00:04:41,506
A failed job needs a diagnosis.

113
00:04:42,086 --> 00:04:45,906
This recording follows a GROMACS simulation on DICC

114
00:04:45,906 --> 00:04:49,026
with an AI assistant helping to interpret

115
00:04:49,026 --> 00:04:50,226
the status reports.

116
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:54,086
The first problem was a launch failure.

117
00:04:54,386 --> 00:04:58,366
OpenMP could not bind its processes to CPU

118
00:04:58,366 --> 00:05:01,926
cores that points to the computing setup rather

119
00:05:01,926 --> 00:05:03,626
than proving molecular instability.

120
00:05:03,626 --> 00:05:07,526
After the launch settings were corrected, the display

121
00:05:07,526 --> 00:05:09,946
update reported that a 16-core

122
00:05:09,946 --> 00:05:13,066
binding check passed and the first 500 ps

123
00:05:13,066 --> 00:05:15,026
of the NPT stage completed.

124
00:05:15,426 --> 00:05:17,906
Those milestones still need the underlying outputs.

125
00:05:18,826 --> 00:05:21,126
Later, the monitoring connection dropped.

126
00:05:21,586 --> 00:05:23,946
The latest progress could no longer be confirmed.

127
00:05:24,566 --> 00:05:27,286
A failed connection does not by itself establish

128
00:05:27,286 --> 00:05:28,446
a failed simulation.

129
00:05:28,446 --> 00:05:31,766
keep the last verified progress separate from the

130
00:05:31,766 --> 00:05:32,886
unknown current state.

131
00:05:33,826 --> 00:05:36,186
Good monitoring makes uncertainty explicit.

132
00:05:36,826 --> 00:05:39,246
An AI assistant can help organize evidence,

133
00:05:39,726 --> 00:05:42,366
distinguish operational problems from simulation behavior,

134
00:05:42,786 --> 00:05:43,946
and guide the next check.

135
00:05:44,726 --> 00:05:46,966
Scientific conclusions depend on the underlying outputs.
